(Headline result) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Across the 41 deployments, median spend on input tokens fell 52% after a cache) Tj T*
(breakpoint was introduced above the system prompt. The interquartile range is wide:) Tj T*
(the 25th percentile saved 31% and the 75th percentile saved 68%.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Breakeven) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A cached prefix pays for itself once it is read roughly 5 times per write. Below that) Tj T*
(the 1.25× write premium is never recovered, and a product that rewrites its prefix on) Tj T*
(every request pays about 25% more than it would have paid with no caching at all.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Sensitivity) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The saving is dominated by the share of the prompt that is static. Deployments whose) Tj T*
(static prefix was under 30% of median prompt length saved less than 15%, whatever) Tj T*
(their hit rate.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
