(The low-hit-rate regime) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Below a 40% cache hit rate the median deployment saved nothing measurable: write) Tj T*
(premiums and read discounts cancelled within the noise of week-to-week traffic. Nine) Tj T*
(of the 41 deployments spent more with caching enabled than they had without it.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Bursty traffic) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Hit rate tracks session density, not request volume. A product with the same daily) Tj T*
(volume spread thinly across time zones sat at a 22% hit rate; the same volume) Tj T*
(concentrated into working hours sat at 71%.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Limitations) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Self-selection is the obvious one. Deployments that switched caching on and saw) Tj T*
(nothing had no incentive to enrol, so the headline figure is an upper bound rather) Tj T*
(than an expectation.) Tj T*
ET
